`xs.map(f)` and `xs.filter(f)` read in a view body, on the Go targets, which
withhold listLambdas.

NoListLambdas used to hoist an accumulator loop ahead of the widget reading the
result. On bubbletea the accumulator was rendered as a view loop, its body
dropped, and the widget reading `[0]` of it panicked on the first frame; fyne
and gtk4 made it a render slot, whose function appended to a list declared in
the build function it could not see. A node's prop is no longer hoisted: the
emitter writes the call as an expression of its own, which a re-render
evaluates again.

deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `part\d+Items` -- an accumulator loop is not a view loop
deny * `__list\d+` -- a prop's map is an expression, not a hoisted accumulator
-- view.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"

func dbl(x int) => x * 2

component main node {
    var xs = [3, 4]
    text(value="{xs.map(dbl)[0]} {xs.filter(func(x int) => x > 3)[0]}")
}

window {
    main
}

output {
    go {
        bubbletea
        fyne
        gtk4
    }
}
